            {
              "id": "3f81374c-cfc1-37a9-8028-fed2b6b112d4",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "This finding is classified as a genuine vulnerability because the analysis identified a risk of undefined behavior due to possible overlap between the source and destination memory regions in the memory copy operation. The destination and source may refer to overlapping memory, as indicated by the dataflow analysis. Additionally, there is no evidence of a guard to ensure the destination pointer is not null, which further increases the risk. The classification explicitly states undefined behavior risk, and the verdict confirms this is a genuine issue. The source is confirmed to be non-null before the call, but the destination may be null, and the overlap is feasible due to dataflow from destination to source.\n\n## In Context Remediation 1\nTo prevent undefined behavior when copying memory regions that may overlap, add a runtime check to ensure the source and destination do not overlap before calling the memory copy function. If overlap is possible, use a safe memory move function that handles overlapping regions correctly.\n\n```cpp\nif (c_A->x != csrVal && !(csrVal > c_A->x && csrVal < (c_A->x + sizeof(double) * nnzA)) && !(c_A->x > csrVal && c_A->x < (csrVal + sizeof(double) * nnzA))) {\n    memcpy(c_A->x, csrVal, sizeof(double) * nnzA);\n} else {\n    memmove(c_A->x, csrVal, sizeof(double) * nnzA);\n}\n```\nThis code checks for overlap and uses `memmove` only if necessary, otherwise it uses `memcpy` for performance.\n\n\n## In Context Remediation 2\nAlternatively, replace the memory copy function with a memory move function that is safe for overlapping memory regions:\n\n```cpp\nmemmove(c_A->x, csrVal, sizeof(double) * nnzA);\n```\nThis ensures correct behavior even if the source and destination memory regions overlap.\n\n## References\n- [OWASP C-Based Toolchain Hardening Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/119.html)\n- [CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/120.html)\n- [CWE-787: Out-of-bounds Write](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/787.html)\n- [OWASP Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n\n\n___\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "DS121708"
