            {
              "id": "c21c3ad7-3766-341b-8ead-aebaca92586f",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "This finding is classified as a genuine vulnerability because the analysis detected a possible undefined behavior risk due to overlapping memory regions in a memory copy operation. The destination and source buffers may overlap, as indicated by the dataflow analysis, which can lead to unpredictable results when using memcpy. Additionally, there is a risk that the destination pointer may be null, as there is no clear guard ensuring it is valid before the call. The source pointer is guarded and cannot be null, but the overlap and potential null destination make this a high-confidence, actionable issue. The classification and verdict both indicate a genuine problem that should be addressed to prevent undefined behavior and potential security vulnerabilities.\n\n## In Context Remediation 1\nBefore performing the memory copy, ensure that the source and destination buffers do not overlap. You can add a runtime check to verify that the memory regions are distinct:\n\n```cpp\nif ((c_A->i != csrColInd) &&\n    ((c_A->i + nnzA <= csrColInd) || (csrColInd + nnzA <= c_A->i))) {\n    memcpy(c_A->i, csrColInd, sizeof(rocblas_int) * nnzA);\n} else {\n    // Handle overlap case or log an error\n}\n```\nThis check ensures that the memory regions do not overlap before calling memcpy. If overlap is possible, handle it appropriately (e.g., use memmove or log an error).\n\n## In Context Remediation 2\nIf overlapping memory regions are possible and must be supported, replace memcpy with memmove, which is safe for overlapping regions:\n\n```cpp\nmemmove(c_A->i, csrColInd, sizeof(rocblas_int) * nnzA);\n```\nThis change ensures correct behavior even if the source and destination buffers overlap.\n\n## References\n- [OWASP C-Based Toolchain Hardening Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/119.html)\n- [CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/120.html)\n- [CWE-787: Out-of-bounds Write](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/787.html)\n- [OWASP Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n\n___\n"
